[center][size=6][b]COMPLETIONIST[/b][/size]
[size=3]Every quest and activity in Starfield, and what you're still missing in each star system, planet and city.[/size][/center]

[size=4][b]What it does[/b][/size]
The game's mission log only shows quests you've already picked up. Completionist knows the full list in advance and tracks your progress automatically:

[list]
[*][b]251 quests and 94 activities[/b] from the base game, [b]Shattered Space[/b], [b]Terran Armada[/b], the [b]Free Lanes[/b] update and the [b]Trackers Alliance[/b]. Content you don't own is skipped automatically.
[*][b]Grouped by place:[/b] see what's left in New Atlantis, Neon, Akila City, Dazra and every other system, planet and city.
[*][b]Here tab:[/b] what's missing where you are standing right now.
[*][b]Questlines:[/b] each faction and the main story as a chain, in story order.
[*][b]Activities:[/b] one-off activities (Earth landmarks, Clinic jobs, space encounters) and the small errands the game counts toward its own Activities stat.
[*][b]Track[/b] a started quest or [b]show its start on the starmap[/b] (plots a course) straight from the menu.
[*][b]Branching choices handled:[/b] choose the Crimson Fleet or UC SysDef ending, take Foreknowledge or the regular path, and the paths you didn't take count as resolved, so 100% is always reachable.
[*][b]New Game+ aware:[/b] the NG+ intro variants count as One Small Step; Among the Stars and Foreknowledge only count once you've entered Unity.
[*][b]Manual override:[/b] mark any quest done or not done if detection gets it wrong (saved in your save).
[*][b]Spoiler mode:[/b] hide the names of quests you haven't discovered.
[*][b]Notifications[/b] when you complete a quest or activity, with that place's progress ("Completed: Superfan (Neon 7/35)").
[*][b]Controller support.[/b]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Controls[/b][/size]
Open the menu with [b]F7[/b] (rebind it in Mod Settings), or from the [b]Pause menu > Mod Settings > Launcher[/b].
[list]
[*]Switch tab: Q / E (LB / RB)
[*]Move: arrow keys (D-pad / left stick); left/right switches between the place list and the quests
[*]Track or show on map: Enter (A); show on map: R (X)
[*]Filter: F (Y) · Spoilers: X (View) · Mark done / not done: M (right-stick click)
[*]Close: Esc (B)
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/106]Starfield Script Extender (SFSE)[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/3256]Address Library for SFSE Plugins[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/18326]OSF Settings[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/17711]OSF UI[/url] (needs the Microsoft Edge WebView2 Runtime, included with Windows 11)
[/list]
Without OSF UI / OSF Settings the tracking and notifications still work; only the menu is unavailable.

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
Install with Vortex or Mod Organizer 2 and enable [b]StarfieldCompletionist.esm[/b]. Launch the game through SFSE. Safe to install mid-playthrough: progress is read from your save.

[size=4][b]Good to know[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Like any mod with a plugin, it disables achievements unless you use an achievement enabler.
[*]Steam version only for the menu (SFSE doesn't support the Game Pass / Microsoft Store version).
[*]Quest places are worked out from where each quest giver stands; a few may be off. Please report them in the Bugs tab.
[/list]

